-- title:
--   Mod-3 lattice module realising the weight-two bridge product
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ (a natural number with `NeZero N`) and assume [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6), i.e. that the $\mathbb{C}$-span of [`CuspForm.intLattice N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the cusp forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients `qCoeff` are rational integers — is the whole space. Let $a:\mathbb{N}\to\mathbb{Z}$ satisfy $a_1=1$ and [`CuspForm.IsLatticeRealized N a`](def/CuspForm_IntegralLattice.html#L27): there is a weight-two cusp form $f$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$ with every `qCoeff f n` in the prime subring of $\mathbb{C}$, and integers $a_f(n)$ with $(a_f(n):\mathbb{C})=$ `qCoeff f n` and $3 \mid a_f(n)-\mathrm{coeff}_n(F)$ for all $n$, where $F=$ [`bridgeProduct a`](def/CuspForm_IntegralLattice.html#L22) is the product of $\sum_n a_n q^n$ with the integral power series `e1Chi3In ℤ`. The assertion is the existence of a type $M$, an abelian group structure on it, a module structure over $\mathbb{T}=$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 {ℓ | ℓ ∣ N}`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$), and a function $\mathrm{red}:\mathbb{Z}[\![X]\!]\to M$ (no additivity required) such that: $\mathrm{red}(g)=0$ whenever $3$ divides every coefficient of $g$; conversely $\mathrm{red}(g)=0$ forces $3\mid\mathrm{coeff}_1(g)$; $3\cdot\mathrm{red}(F)=0$ in $M$; and for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ (where $\ell\nmid N$ simultaneously serves as the condition $\ell\notin\{\ell\mid\ell\mid N\}$ needed for $T_\ell\in\mathbb{T}$), $(T_\ell-a_\ell)\cdot\mathrm{red}(F)=\mathrm{red}\big(T_\ell^{\mathrm{formal}}F-a_\ell F\big)$, with $T_\ell^{\mathrm{formal}}=U_\ell+\ell\,V_\ell$ the formal weight-two Hecke operator [`PowerSeries.heckeT ℓ 2`](def/PowerSeries_FormalHeckeOperators.html#L33) on power series.
--
--   This packages the mod-$3$ reduction of the integral lattice in $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$, together with its stability under the integral Hecke algebra, as an abstract datum: a $\mathbb{T}$-module with a reduction map from integral $q$-expansions detecting divisibility by $3$ in the first coefficient and intertwining the formal and geometric Hecke actions on the bridge product. It is used by [`FLT.AbstractIntegralStructure.exists_weight_two_eigenform_congruent_of_heckeT_congr`](thm.html#FLT.AbstractIntegralStructure.exists_weight_two_eigenform_congruent_of_heckeT_congr) in the passage from a weight-one form twisted by $E_1(\chi_{-3})$ to a weight-two eigenform congruent to it modulo $3$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_reductionModule_of_isLatticeRealized.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_IntegralStructure
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_IntegralLattice
